        <h3>In-person classes</h3>
        <p>Small-group, hands-on classes in cities across India. Cook together, taste together, and walk out with recipes you can repeat the same week.</p>
        <span class="more">Upcoming dates announced on the contact page.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Online cooking courses</h3>
        <p>Video-led courses you can follow at your own pace, designed for the home cook with a normal Indian kitchen and pantry — no fancy equipment.</p>
        <span class="more">Available year-round.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--paper); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <h2>What you will be able to make</h2>
    <ul class="checks">
      <li>Whole-grain breakfasts that don't crash your energy by eleven.</li>
      <li>Dals, sabzis and one-pot meals that feel familiar and feel light.</li>
      <li>Plant-based "dairy" — milks, curds and cheeses — from nuts and seeds.</li>
      <li>Sweets and snacks that genuinely qualify as healthy.</li>
      <li>Travel and lunchbox food that holds up away from a kitchen.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who teaches</h2>
    <p>Classes are led by SHARAN-trained chefs and educators, with input from our medical and nutrition team. The focus is on food that is delicious first and healthy second — because if it isn't tasty, none of this lasts.</p>

